ave JC Penney and Macy's and we  didn't have the big Black Friday sales  like they do here in the States and it  was always my dream to go to one of  those in 2007 my husband and I moved to  Florida and  I met some friends I was like can we  please do the Black Friday thing it's  been a bit of a weird dream of mine so  we did and it was fun and we had a great  time and we did that for a couple years  when I look at it now it's just so sad  how much money is spent and people are  hurt at these sales and sometimes killed  at these sales and for what we're  running around buying stuff we don't  need and and can't afford and it just  doesn't really make sense since we live  out here on the west coast it's been  really hard to send anything home to my  family it's just really expensive and  since we've lived here we decided not to  send anything for Christmas and not to  exchange gifts and really you know my  dad's older and and so my sister and I  and and our kids are in their teens and  20s and none of us really need anything  so we just didn't see the point since  we've lived here the kids and I go to  the Thanksgiving Day Parade in Seattle  on Black Friday and we go to the parade  and then afterwards what we do is we  hand out lunches to people that are on  the streets the homeless people on the  streets who there are a lot of here in  Seattle it's really sad and we make up  turkey sandwiches and we have an orange  and a bottle of water and like cookies  and stuff and last year we also  collected scarves and gloves and we hand  them out to the homeless people and I  think it's been really great to show my  kids that you know it's important to  give to people that just don't have  things and just are less fortunate than  us so it's been really good so we're  gonna do that again this year and my dad  and my sister last year for Christmas  they actually went to the local police  station to talk to some of the officers  and just find out if there were some  needy familie